  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The General Services Administration obligated $20.6B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration recorded 988,683 awards with an average award size of $20.9K. Obligations are down 13.3% year over year. Yearly obligations have varied: FY21 totaled $17.7B, FY22 totaled $20.6B, FY23 totaled $23.9B, FY24 totaled $26.5B, and FY25 totaled $23.8B. The largest categories of spending in FY2026 to date are Computer Systems Design Services at $4.3B and Engineering Services at $3.6B, followed by Automobile Manufacturing at $2.3B. The General Services Administration’s top vendors in FY2026 to date include BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $1.8B and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $890M. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date. This snapshot shows where the General Services Administration is buying most of its services and which suppliers are receiving the largest contract obligations so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2026 obligations compare with prior years?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $20.6B in FY2026 to date, which is down 13.3% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a peak at $26.5B in FY24 and a decline to $23.8B in FY25 before the current FY26 total of $20.6B. The General Services Administration’s FY21 and FY22 totals were $17.7B and $20.6B respectively, showing that FY26 to date matches FY22 but remains below the FY24 peak. These totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial for the current year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is the General Services Administration concentrating its spending in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services lead obligations at $4.3B and $3.6B respectively. Automobile Manufacturing is the next-largest category at $2.3B, followed by several professional services and R&D categories including a $1.3B category for Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and $1.2B for All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services. The top vendors receiving the largest obligations include BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC at $1.8B and SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $890M."
      }
    ]
  },
